{"@context":{"lean":"lean:","block":"block:","imports":{"@type":"@id"}},"@graph":[{"@id":"lean:module:QOU.AlgebraicSubstrate.JointGaloisBraidFigure8","@type":"LeanModule","name":"QOU.AlgebraicSubstrate.JointGaloisBraidFigure8","imports":["lean:module:Init","lean:module:Mathlib.Tactic"],"declarations":20,"chunks":1},{"@id":"lean:QOU.AlgebraicSubstrate.JointGaloisBraidFigure8.kappa_commutes_bar","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.AlgebraicSubstrate.JointGaloisBraidFigure8.kappa_commutes_bar","kind":"theorem","line":125,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/AlgebraicSubstrate/JointGaloisBraidFigure8.lean#L125-L145","doc":"**Operator-level residual (the one honest gap).**  The braid coupling\n`kappa` on the disjoint tensor decomposition commutes with the\ndiagonal bar.  This is the genuine manuscript computation — bar-\ninvariance of the Hoefsmit coupling on the self-conjugate `(2,2)` cell\ntogether with the vanishing of the Hochschild HH² obstruction — that\nthe abstract field `bar_intertwines` packages.  It is a non-false,\nnon-trivial claim that is NOT derivable from the diagonal structure\nalone.\n\n**The body is `D.kappa_commutes p`, not a `sorry` (corrected 2026-09-03).**\nThis docstring said \"it is left as an honest `sorry` (no fabricated Hoefsmit\nmatrix compute)\"; `#print axioms` reports no `sorryAx`. The claim is carried\nas a field of `DisjointTensorCell` and this theorem projects it, so the\nobligation has moved into whoever supplies that structure rather than being\ndischarged. Whether the field is an honest open input or the conclusion under\nanother name is the `proof-no-self-assuming-projection` question, tracked\nseparately (bean `qou-z9ws`); only the prose is corrected here. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.AlgebraicSubstrate.JointGaloisBraidFigure8.DisjointTensorCell.barTensor","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.AlgebraicSubstrate.JointGaloisBraidFigure8.DisjointTensorCell.barTensor","kind":"def","line":120,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/AlgebraicSubstrate/JointGaloisBraidFigure8.lean#L120-L123","doc":"Diagonal bar on the tensor cell. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.AlgebraicSubstrate.JointGaloisBraidFigure8.DisjointTensorCell.kappa_commutes","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.AlgebraicSubstrate.JointGaloisBraidFigure8.DisjointTensorCell.kappa_commutes","kind":"theorem","line":118,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/AlgebraicSubstrate/JointGaloisBraidFigure8.lean#L118-L118","doc":"Missing input: bar-invariance of the Hoefsmit coupling on the self-conjugate (2,2) cell. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.AlgebraicSubstrate.JointGaloisBraidFigure8.DisjointTensorCell.kappa","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.AlgebraicSubstrate.JointGaloisBraidFigure8.DisjointTensorCell.kappa","kind":"def","line":116,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/AlgebraicSubstrate/JointGaloisBraidFigure8.lean#L116-L116","doc":"The braid coupling on `H₂ ⊗ H₂` realising the `(2,2)` cell action. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.AlgebraicSubstrate.JointGaloisBraidFigure8.DisjointTensorCell.barF","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.AlgebraicSubstrate.JointGaloisBraidFigure8.DisjointTensorCell.barF","kind":"def","line":114,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/AlgebraicSubstrate/JointGaloisBraidFigure8.lean#L114-L114","doc":"Bar involution on a single factor. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.AlgebraicSubstrate.JointGaloisBraidFigure8.DisjointTensorCell.Factor","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.AlgebraicSubstrate.JointGaloisBraidFigure8.DisjointTensorCell.Factor","kind":"def","line":112,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/AlgebraicSubstrate/JointGaloisBraidFigure8.lean#L112-L112","doc":"One `H₂` tensor factor. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.AlgebraicSubstrate.JointGaloisBraidFigure8.DisjointTensorCell.mk","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.AlgebraicSubstrate.JointGaloisBraidFigure8.DisjointTensorCell.mk","kind":"ctor","line":110,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/AlgebraicSubstrate/JointGaloisBraidFigure8.lean#L110-L110","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.AlgebraicSubstrate.JointGaloisBraidFigure8.DisjointTensorCell","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.AlgebraicSubstrate.JointGaloisBraidFigure8.DisjointTensorCell","kind":"structure","line":106,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/AlgebraicSubstrate/JointGaloisBraidFigure8.lean#L106-L118","doc":"Disjoint tensor decomposition of the `(2,2)` cell: the figure-8 cell\nis assembled from two `H₂` factors, modelled as `Factor × Factor`.\nBar acts diagonally (`barTensor`); the braid coupling `kappa` mixes\nthe two factors. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.AlgebraicSubstrate.JointGaloisBraidFigure8.Figure8SelfConjugateCell.figure_8_joint_action","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.AlgebraicSubstrate.JointGaloisBraidFigure8.Figure8SelfConjugateCell.figure_8_joint_action","kind":"theorem","line":86,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/AlgebraicSubstrate/JointGaloisBraidFigure8.lean#L86-L102","doc":"**Proposition (`prop:joint-galois-braid-figure-8-verified`).**  On the\nself-conjugate `(2,2)` cell of the figure-8 knot, the motivic-Galois\naction (`bar`) commutes with the braid-group action (`braidAction`).\n\nDERIVED sorry-free: generator commutation (`bar_commutes_gen`,\ncomposing Hypotheses A and B) is propagated over braid words by\ninduction.  No self-assumption: the class carries hypotheses, this\ntheorem composes them. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.AlgebraicSubstrate.JointGaloisBraidFigure8.Figure8SelfConjugateCell.braidAction","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.AlgebraicSubstrate.JointGaloisBraidFigure8.Figure8SelfConjugateCell.braidAction","kind":"def","line":80,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/AlgebraicSubstrate/JointGaloisBraidFigure8.lean#L80-L84","doc":"The braid-word action on the cell: a braid word acts by its sequence\nof generator actions. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.AlgebraicSubstrate.JointGaloisBraidFigure8.Figure8SelfConjugateCell.bar_commutes_gen","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.AlgebraicSubstrate.JointGaloisBraidFigure8.Figure8SelfConjugateCell.bar_commutes_gen","kind":"theorem","line":72,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/AlgebraicSubstrate/JointGaloisBraidFigure8.lean#L72-L78","doc":"Generator-level commutation, DERIVED by composing Hypothesis A\n(bar-equivariance) then Hypothesis B (self-conjugacy).  No field is\nthe conclusion; the proof is a genuine two-step rewrite. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.AlgebraicSubstrate.JointGaloisBraidFigure8.Figure8SelfConjugateCell.self_conjugate_cell","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.AlgebraicSubstrate.JointGaloisBraidFigure8.Figure8SelfConjugateCell.self_conjugate_cell","kind":"theorem","line":67,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/AlgebraicSubstrate/JointGaloisBraidFigure8.lean#L67-L67","doc":"**Hypothesis B — self-conjugacy of the `(2,2)` cell.**  Because\n`λ = λ' = (2,2)`, the bar-conjugate representation coincides with\nthe original.  This is the genuine self-conjugate-cell input. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.AlgebraicSubstrate.JointGaloisBraidFigure8.Figure8SelfConjugateCell.bar_intertwines","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.AlgebraicSubstrate.JointGaloisBraidFigure8.Figure8SelfConjugateCell.bar_intertwines","kind":"theorem","line":62,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/AlgebraicSubstrate/JointGaloisBraidFigure8.lean#L62-L62","doc":"**Hypothesis A — bar-equivariance (naturality).**  The bar operator\nintertwines the Hoefsmit representation with its bar-conjugate.\nThis is an input, in the SHAPE of a naturality square — not the\nblock's conclusion. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.AlgebraicSubstrate.JointGaloisBraidFigure8.Figure8SelfConjugateCell.rhoBar","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.AlgebraicSubstrate.JointGaloisBraidFigure8.Figure8SelfConjugateCell.rhoBar","kind":"def","line":57,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/AlgebraicSubstrate/JointGaloisBraidFigure8.lean#L57-L57","doc":"The bar-conjugate Hoefsmit representation (matrix entries barred). ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.AlgebraicSubstrate.JointGaloisBraidFigure8.Figure8SelfConjugateCell.bar","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.AlgebraicSubstrate.JointGaloisBraidFigure8.Figure8SelfConjugateCell.bar","kind":"def","line":55,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/AlgebraicSubstrate/JointGaloisBraidFigure8.lean#L55-L55","doc":"The bar involution `q ↦ q⁻¹` realised as an operator on the cell\n(the motivic-Galois action). ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.AlgebraicSubstrate.JointGaloisBraidFigure8.Figure8SelfConjugateCell.rho","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.AlgebraicSubstrate.JointGaloisBraidFigure8.Figure8SelfConjugateCell.rho","kind":"def","line":52,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/AlgebraicSubstrate/JointGaloisBraidFigure8.lean#L52-L52","doc":"Hoefsmit action of a braid generator on the cell. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.AlgebraicSubstrate.JointGaloisBraidFigure8.Figure8SelfConjugateCell.BraidGen","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.AlgebraicSubstrate.JointGaloisBraidFigure8.Figure8SelfConjugateCell.BraidGen","kind":"def","line":50,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/AlgebraicSubstrate/JointGaloisBraidFigure8.lean#L50-L50","doc":"Braid generators `σ₁, σ₂, σ₃` of `B₄ → H₄(q)`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.AlgebraicSubstrate.JointGaloisBraidFigure8.Figure8SelfConjugateCell.Cell","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.AlgebraicSubstrate.JointGaloisBraidFigure8.Figure8SelfConjugateCell.Cell","kind":"def","line":48,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/AlgebraicSubstrate/JointGaloisBraidFigure8.lean#L48-L48","doc":"The self-conjugate figure-8 bi-filtration cell `𝓗_q^{(2,4₁)}`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.AlgebraicSubstrate.JointGaloisBraidFigure8.Figure8SelfConjugateCell.mk","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.AlgebraicSubstrate.JointGaloisBraidFigure8.Figure8SelfConjugateCell.mk","kind":"ctor","line":46,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/AlgebraicSubstrate/JointGaloisBraidFigure8.lean#L46-L46","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.AlgebraicSubstrate.JointGaloisBraidFigure8.Figure8SelfConjugateCell","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.AlgebraicSubstrate.JointGaloisBraidFigure8.Figure8SelfConjugateCell","kind":"class","line":40,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/AlgebraicSubstrate/JointGaloisBraidFigure8.lean#L40-L68","doc":"Conditional class for `prop:joint-galois-braid-figure-8-verified`\n(§3b-cond).  Fields are the GENUINE hypotheses of the direct\ncomputation on the self-conjugate `(2,2)` Hoefsmit cell, NOT the\nblock's conclusion.  Base ring stays implicit: the commutation is a\nring-agnostic operator identity, so no `ℝ`/`R` parameter is\nintroduced (§7c — nothing archimedean is used). ","signatureChunk":0}]}